---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About — Margins"
  description="Margins is a small, slow tech blog. Essays, notes, and thoughts on the tools we build and live inside."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-20 sm:py-28">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-muted-foreground">
      Colophon
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-serif text-5xl leading-tight tracking-tight">
      A small, slow place to think out loud.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose-blog mt-10">
      <p>
        Margins is a personal tech blog. It exists because the timelines are loud
        and the group chats are louder, and sometimes a thought needs a page to
        stretch out on.
      </p>
      <p>
        You'll find essays here — the kind that take a week to write and ten minutes
        to read. You'll also find notes, reviews, and half-formed thoughts I haven't
        finished arguing with yet. Everything is dated. Nothing is final.
      </p>
      <h2>What it's about</h2>
      <p>
        Software, mostly. The craft of making it, the strangeness of using it, the
        quiet ways it reshapes our days. Occasional detours into keyboards, type,
        and the long history of people trying to write things down.
      </p>
      <h2>What it isn't</h2>
      <p>
        A newsletter funnel. A content engine. A personal brand. There is no signup
        form because there is nothing to sign up for. Come back when you feel like
        it.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        Write the post you wish someone else had written, then go for a walk.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
